      "decision": "The local identifier `ViewportRuler` in this source is bound to the imported `_LegacyViewport` alias from the package-owned `legacy-core` entry point. The maintained TypeScript source helper confirms one alias, one constructor type reference, the expected supplied-instance forwarding position where applicable, and no peer `@angular/cdk/scrolling:ViewportRuler` import. The installed peer symbol is documented `@docs-private` in the retained prior source review; this row does not claim it as a stable public API. The fixture correction is an unrelated progress-bar default-token identity assertion (`!==` to `===`) in the packed-consumer producer. It does not alter any viewport source, viewport fixture setup, or viewport assertion semantics. The corrected consumer harness checks that `mat-select` and `mat-tab-header` injector lookups share the same owned `_LegacyViewport` instance and that its width/height match `window.innerWidth`/`window.innerHeight`. The same packed artifact has a retained RxJS 6.5.3 minimum consumer receipt with 106/106 consumer cases. These receipts support only those actual harness observations and do not make a complete `ViewportRuler` behavioral, platform, or G11 claim.",
